I think you are overthinking the concept.  One man's dog food is another's 
cuisine.  For example, Russians eat horse meat and think nothing of it.  
When I was in Ukraine visiting my in-laws, I was eating some yummy sausage 
which I found out later to be made from horseflesh.  I almost gagged, not 
because it was bad sausage, but because I grew up associating horsemeat 
with dog food.

As for tripe, I had a bad experience with menudo as a child growing up in 
Tucson, AZ.  Our neighbors ate it regularly, my sister and I played with 
the kids, but when their dad was making menudo (it turned out he was the 
worst Mexican chef in the Southwest) the smell was too much for me to 
bear.

